# game-engine-algorithms

Core game engine algorithms focus on therapeutic social skills development through a specialized token-based evaluation system and adaptive difficulty scaling.

## Scoring System
Implementation Path: real-world-decisions/js/game.js

Token-based evaluation using three-tier scoring:
- Green tokens: 5 points (optimal decisions)
- Yellow tokens: 3 points (acceptable decisions)
- Red tokens: 1 point (needs improvement)

## Difficulty Scaling
Progressive difficulty adjustment based on resident performance metrics:
- Automatically scales scenario complexity
- Adapts to demonstrated social competency levels
- Integrates with behavioral assessment workflows

## Assessment Framework 
Six-step therapeutic evaluation process:
1. Problem Identification
2. Options Analysis  
3. Consequence Evaluation
4. Impact Assessment
5. Decision Making 
6. Action Planning

## Game Modes
Specialized therapeutic modes:
- Standard Challenge: Basic skill development path
- Tournament: Competitive reinforcement
- Skill Building: Focused competency training 
- Quick Decision: Crisis response scenarios

## Scenario Categories
Implementation Path: real-world-decisions/js/data.js

Structured life skill categories:
- Everyday Choices
- Social Situations 
- School & Work
- Family Relationships
- Money Management
- Health & Safety

Each scenario contains:
- Multiple difficulty tiers
- Social skill classification tags
- Defined learning outcomes
- Behavioral assessment metrics

